-- title:
--   Supersingular component chart over a supersingular place: existence and uniqueness
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, and write $\kappa$ for its residue field. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\kappa$-algebra `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of $j$ and of its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion) whose members are exactly the elements of `ssPlaces q M' κ`, namely the places $w$ that are $\kappa$-rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and have $w$-value of `jGeomGen κ M'` in `ssJSet q κ`. Assume `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` — the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` — is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with reduced field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` contracting to $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction on $A$, together with the scaling and place-map axioms of `ConstantReduction`; assume moreover that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue equal, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, to its coefficientwise reduction. Then for every $s\in W$ there are a field $\mathrm{FSS}$ with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and a component chart $C$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with reduced field $\mathrm{FSS}$ such that: (i) some element of $\mathrm{FSS}$ is transcendental over $\kappa$; (ii) $C$ lies over $s$, in the sense that for every $R_0$-integral $f\in$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` satisfying $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f\ge 0$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$ has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `C.integers` and its $C$-residue is the image in $\mathrm{FSS}$ of the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$; (iii) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and every $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, the pullback of $C$ along the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` has the same integers as $C$, i.e. `C.integers` is stable under that automorphism; and (iv) these properties pin down the valuation subring: any field $F'$ over $\kappa$ and component chart $C'$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with reduced field $F'$ satisfying (i), (ii) and (iii) has `C'.integers = C.integers`.
--
--   This is the intrinsic characterisation of the supersingular (Drinfeld) component of the stable reduction of the modular curve of level $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ at $q$ sitting over the supersingular point $s$: it is specified by lying over $s$, by invariance under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, and by uniqueness, with no model or tame extension appearing in the statement. It feeds the assembly of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve used in the descent and inertia-at-infinity arguments.
